1
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:58,000
The Battle is over. The War has just begun!

2
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Puppet Master X: Axis Rising is a horror, war, science
fiction film directed by Charles Band.

3
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:42,000
After foiling a plan to blow up an American arms plant, Danny and Beth quickly find that one of Toulon's puppets has been
kidnapped by the Nazis, and his life-giving serum has been synthesized to create a master race of unstoppable soldiers.

4
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:34,000
Danny, played by Kip Canyon.

5
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:26,000
Beth, played by Jean Louise O'Sullivan.

6
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Freuhoffer, played by Oto Brezina.

7
00:41:04,000 --> 00:41:10,000
Uschi, played by Stephanie Sanditz.

8
00:46:56,000 --> 00:47:02,000
Sgt. Stone, played by Brad Potts.

9
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
Ozu, played by Terumi Shimazu.

10
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
Puppet Master X: Axis Rising is a 2012 American horror film and is
the tenth entry in the Puppet Master film series.

11
01:04:32,000 --> 01:04:38,000
Produced and directed by Charles Band, it is a direct sequel to 2010's Puppet Master: Axis of Evil and introduces
new puppets named Blitzkrieg, Bombshell, Kamikaze, and Weremacht, who fight alongside the Nazis.

12
01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:30,000
Puppet Master X: Axis Rising was released on
October 9, 2012 by Full Moon Features.

13
01:16:16,000 --> 01:16:22,000
A sequel, Puppet Master: Axis Termination, was released in 2017.

14
01:22:08,000 --> 01:22:14,000
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
